The source retains Apache License 2.0. QuiFox changes package wiring, application storage
paths, and adds annotation/plugin integration. No ZCode application, model, login,
telemetry, service, or GUI implementation is imported.
QuiFox also restricts the inherited child environment. Vendored source retains upstream
formatting and its own strict TypeScript build; repository ESLint style rules do not
rewrite third-party algorithms.
QuiFox narrows its author-facing facade to Agent asks, arguments, phase labels and logs.
An opt-in control-view projection follows completed awaits rather than retaining
the asynchronous spawner cursor as an apparent bypass path. Execution is unchanged.
QuiFox additionally instruments annotated function bodies and traces their actual
parent/child invocations using asynchronous call contexts. Its default UI graph is
a TypeScript symbol-resolved call graph, separate from upstream control-flow projections.
